        {
          "id": "495e5abb-3fe3-45bc-a701-3c29ebcf98d8",
          "name": "Get Event Preread",
          "request": {
            "name": "Get Event Preread",
            "description": {
              "content": "Generate or dispatch a pre-read for an upcoming calendar event.\n\nThe desktop already has Google's ``external_id`` from the sync payload, so\ncallers identify the event by that string rather than the internal UUID.\nThe query layer scopes by ``user_id`` — a stranger's ``external_id``\nmatches no row.\n\nWhen ``useAgenticPreread`` is false (the default), the handler\nsynchronously builds context and calls the LLM; the worst case is bounded\nby the generator's 30s Anthropic client timeout.\n\nWhen ``useAgenticPreread`` is true, the handler dispatches a managed-agent\nsession in the background and returns an empty response immediately. The\ndesktop picks up the deliverable via the ``agentic_prereads`` sync resource once\nthe webhook completes.\n\nEvents that already ended are fetch-only: the latest stored pre-read is\nreturned as-is, and nothing is ever generated or dispatched for them.\n\nReturns 404 only when the event isn't eligible for a pre-read at all:\n\n* No CalendarEvent for ``(user_id, external_id)``.\n* The event is cancelled.\n* The event already ended and has no stored pre-read.\n\nWhen the event exists but the LLM-side generator fails (rate limits,\nvalidation errors, transient outages), the response is still 200 with\na minimal calendar-derived fallback so the desktop can render the\npre-read card with baseline metadata instead of an empty failure\nstate. The generator already logged + counted the failure.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "calendar",
                "events",
                ":external_id",
                "preread"
              ],
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "useAgenticPreread",
                  "value": "false",
                  "description": "When true, dispatch a managed-agent pre-read session asynchronously and return an empty response. The desktop picks up the result via the ``agentic_prereads`` sync resource."
                },
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "key": "trigger",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "description": "Optional client-supplied hint describing why the pre-read is being fetched. Allowed values: precache, reminder, debug, sync. Used for telemetry only — unknown values fall through silently."
                }
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "disabled": false,
                  "type": "any",
                  "value": "<string>",
                  "key": "external_id",
                  "description": "(Required) "
                }
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "apikey",
              "apikey": [
                {
                  "key": "key",
                  "value": "Authorization"
                },
                {
                  "key": "value",
                  "value": "{{apiKey}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "in",
                  "value": "header"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
